            <ArticleTitle>Cardiopulmonary rehabilitation and cancer rehabilitation. 3. Cancer rehabilitation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S65-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">This self-directed learning module highlights the treatment and rehabilitation of patients with cancer. It is part of the study guide on cardiac, pulmonary, and cancer rehabilitation in the Self-Directed Physiatric Education Program for practitioners and trainees in physical medicine and rehabilitation. This article reviews medical and rehabilitation issues in patients with various types of cancer. Cases were selected to allow discussion of problems seen in both younger and older patient populations. Identification of common sequelae of cancer and cancer treatments, associated rehabilitation challenges, and appropriate interventions are included.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OVERALL ARTICLE OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To summarize the medical and rehabilitation issues in patients with various types of cancer.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
